# Cloudflare Pages global headers.
# Per-route OG share-card endpoints return SVG bodies but Pages was
# auto-coercing the Content-Type to text/html on Functions responses,
# which broke link-preview consumers (Twitter, Slack, email scrapers).
# Force the SVG content-type here so the share cards render correctly.
/og/*
  Content-Type: image/svg+xml; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=3600

# Vite writes every build output under dist/assets/ with a content hash in
# the filename by default (vite.config.ts sets no assetFileNames/
# chunkFileNames/assetsDir override, so this is stock Vite 8 behavior); a
# changed file gets a new name, it never overwrites the old one at the same
# path. public/ has no assets/ subfolder, so nothing non-hashed can land at
# this path and inherit the rule. Safe to cache forever ONLY because
# functions/assets/[[path]].ts turns the SPA fallback into a 404 no-store: on
# its own, Pages answers a missing chunk with index.html as 200 text/html, and
# this rule would stamp THAT immutable too -- which cached an HTML document
# under a chunk URL in the PI's browser for a year and blanked the portal
# (2026-09-14). A stale tab's old chunk now 404s (lazyRoute reloads it).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
